  "question": "For an https:// URL, libcurl may race a first connection attempt over HTTP/3 against a second attempt over HTTP/2. In an ngtcp2 build, how does the HTTP/3 attempt's 'has the server replied yet' signal reach the racing logic, and how does it affect when the HTTP/2 attempt is started?\n\nBuild assumptions: USE_NGTCP2 and USE_NGHTTP3 plus nghttp2; OpenSSL; CURLOPT_HTTP_VERSION set so that the first attempt is h3 and the second h2 (e.g. CURL_HTTP_VERSION_3 with fallback allowed); no HTTPS-RR records; no proxy; non-Windows.",
